[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 1 > **UE AI Game Programming (EN)** - 3 ECTS]
# Cours Programme 2026/2027  
## Semestre 1  
### **UE AI Game Programming (EN)** - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: M. Regin
- This course presents different techniques to program games for one or two players. For two-player games, only full information games will be considered.
- The students will have to develop, in groups of two, a program that will simulate a human player.
A competition between the programs will be organized and it will determine the notes.

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 1 > **UE AI: Models and Applications** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **UE AI: Models and Applications** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: M. Enrico
- The main goal of the course is to introduce the students to the different concepts of machine learning by neural networks (also several other models will be considered). For most subjects, first the formal aspects and concepts will be introduced and explained, then they will be illustrated through a series of programming exercises and experiments.
- [https://upinfo.univ-cotedazur.fr/s1/AI-models/](https://upinfo.univ-cotedazur.fr/s1/AI-models/)

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 2 > **UE Combinatorial Optimization** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **UE Combinatorial Optimization** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: M. Regin
- This course presents greedy algorithms, decision diagrams, and markov models.

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 1 > **Web** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **Web** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: M. Buffa
- It has also become a “social machine” and a technological
infrastructure for collective intelligence, which constitutes an
interesting and complex subject of study.
The objective of this course is to provide a comprehensive introduction
to the architecture, standards, languages, and models that allow this
huge distributed system to function, without forgetting its societal
impact.
- Lectures
- The Web’s Architecture and protocols
- A refresher on HTML, CSS, and the Document Object Model
- The Common Gateway Interface and Server-side Programming
- Client-side Programming (JavaScript and the HTML5 API)
- Persistence, AJAX, and REST
- An introduction to Web Services, UDDI, and SOAP
- Ergonomy
- Web Science: The Web as an object of study.

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 1 > **UE Neural Language Processing** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **UE Neural Language Processing** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: Mme. Ollagnier
- This course offers a modern introduction to how machines understand and generate information by connecting data, representation, and learning. We begin with the foundations: how raw data is transformed into meaningful numerical forms through embeddings and how these representations populate latent spaces where similarity, structure, and meaning can be analyzed mathematically. We then explore the evolution of sequence modeling—from the early days of Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs) to the emergence of Transformers, the architecture that now powers today’s Large Language Models (LLMs) such as GPT, BERT, and T5. Along the way, students will discover how attention mechanisms replaced recurrence and enabled models to scale, reason, and generalize. Finally, the course emphasizes practical skills in data analysis and visualization, enabling you to interpret model behavior, examine embedding spaces, and better understand how language models structure and transform information.

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 1 > **UE Software Engineering Software engineering and Design patterns**(EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **UE Software Engineering Software engineering and Design patterns**(EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: Leturc, Regin

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 2 > **Modelling Distributed Systems**(EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **Modelling Distributed Systems**(EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Mme. Di Giusto
- The aim of this course is to introduce mathematical formalisms for modelling and reasoning about properties of distributed, reactive systems.
Topics may include models of message passing and shared memory concurrency (Petri nets, process algebras, communicating and timed automata) as well as formalisms to reason on such systems (bisimulation techniques, session types, logics, invariants…).

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 1 > **Problem Solving** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **Problem Solving** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: Mme. Pelleau
- This course aims to demonstrate how real-life problems can be solved, such as gate allocation for airplanes, constrained pathfinding, etc. Various types of methods will be presented, such as greedy algorithms, local search, and constraint programming.
- This course is divided into 4 main parts:
1. Modelization
2. Greedy Algorithms
3. Local Search
4. Constraint Programming

