[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 1 > **UE Neural Language Processing** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **UE Neural Language Processing** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: Mme. Ollagnier
- This course offers a modern introduction to how machines understand and generate information by connecting data, representation, and learning. We begin with the foundations: how raw data is transformed into meaningful numerical forms through embeddings and how these representations populate latent spaces where similarity, structure, and meaning can be analyzed mathematically. We then explore the evolution of sequence modeling—from the early days of Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs) to the emergence of Transformers, the architecture that now powers today’s Large Language Models (LLMs) such as GPT, BERT, and T5. Along the way, students will discover how attention mechanisms replaced recurrence and enabled models to scale, reason, and generalize. Finally, the course emphasizes practical skills in data analysis and visualization, enabling you to interpret model behavior, examine embedding spaces, and better understand how language models structure and transform information.

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 2 > **UE Natural Language Processing** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
## Semestre 2  
### **UE Natural Language Processing** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: Mme. Cabrio

---

. This program covers both theoretical foundations and practical implementations through projects and real-world case studies. Objectives and fields of application: i) Introduction to Natural Language Processing: Understanding the basic concepts of NLP and its applications in various fields, including information retrieval and information extraction; 2) Text Classification: Exploration of supervised classification methods to automatically organize and categorize texts based on their content; 3) Sentiment Analysis: Techniques for identifying and quantifying emotions and opinions expressed in texts, using supervised learning models; 4) Information Extraction: Methods for automatically identifying and extracting relevant data from large amounts of unstructured text.

---

[Context: Cours Programme 2026/2027 > Semestre 1 > **UE AI: Models and Applications** (EN) - 3 ECTS]
### **UE AI: Models and Applications** (EN) - 3 ECTS  
- Lecteur: M. Enrico
- The main goal of the course is to introduce the students to the different concepts of machine learning by neural networks (also several other models will be considered). For most subjects, first the formal aspects and concepts will be introduced and explained, then they will be illustrated through a series of programming exercises and experiments.
- [https://upinfo.univ-cotedazur.fr/s1/AI-models/](https://upinfo.univ-cotedazur.fr/s1/AI-models/)

